#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# real_abs

#% text
# `real_abs(x)` gives the absolute value of a real number `x`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# Symbolic and complex arguments stay unevaluated.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
real_abs(-3)
#% output
#= 3

#% cell
real_abs(2.5)
#% output
#= 2.5

#% cell
real_abs(e - 3)
#% output
#= 3 - e

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `abs`, `real_sign`
